(:id "go/R11" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/gotable/fixed_r11_c14_test.go: TestGoFixedArrayBoundsAndLiveExtents/writer-bounds-per-plan" "internal/codegen/gotable/fixed_r11_c14_test.go: TestGoFixedArrayBoundsAndLiveExtentsNegativeControl/writer-bounds-per-plan") :note "2026-11-09: closed under the one read. The plan compiled for the OLD [..4] writer refuses a forged count 5 (past the writer's 4, inside the distractor [..6]'s 6 and the reader's own 8); the same 5 reads clean under the [..6] peer's plan, so the bound is per plan and per writer. The negative control plants the count bound in the emitted runtime and requires the refusal to go red on count_over_bound. The old TestFixedVersioningWriterBoundCount check that a named refusal is not Refused() was the stale line; it now asserts the counters and damage class only.")
(:id "go/C14" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/gotable/fixed_r11_c14_test.go: TestGoFixedArrayBoundsAndLiveExtents/live-extents" "internal/codegen/gotable/fixed_r11_c14_test.go: TestGoFixedArrayBoundsAndLiveExtentsNegativeControl/live-extents") :note "2026-11-09: closed under the one read. The read-side bounds walk a counted array's live count only: out-of-range int32s, a 0x02 bool byte and text bytes past the used length in the declared slack are ignored, and the live prefix reads with an empty report. The negative control widens the emitted loop to the declared bound and requires the read to go red on the live extent.")
