(:id "vt/wire-fuzzer/go" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/gotable/wirefuzz_verdict_test.go: TestGoWireFuzzVerdictPipe" "internal/codegen/gotable/wirefuzz_verdict_test.go: TestGoWireFuzzVerdictPipeNegativeControl") :note "2026-11-09: closed under the one read. The Go emitter holds the strict read across the region, retaining and builder wire-fuzz verdict pipes: an empty fixed-form file on a single-record root load refuses as truncated, a node record of a type the reader cannot name is wire-checked after the node directory is populated, a body with bytes past its terminating zero ref refuses as wire_damaged, unknown keyed-array slots and unknown union arms run tableWireSkipFramed and mark any pointer targets inside them, retaining capture wire-checks and marks pointer targets inside unknown fields, and blobs referenced from unknown fields or records are tracked for shared-blob and unreferenced-blob refusals. TestGoWireFuzzVerdictPipe drives the verdict pipe in plain, --retain and --builder modes; TestGoWireFuzzVerdictPipeNegativeControl plants faults in the real generated Go artifacts and requires the verdict pipe to fail.")
